  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<p>C</p>\n<p>The energy of the emitted photon is the difference between the initial and final energy levels, ΔE = <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{\\mathrm{initial}}\"></span> - <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{\\mathrm{final}}\"></span> = E₄ - E₂ = -3.9 eV - (-8.7 eV) = 4.8 eV. This energy must be converted to Joules by multiplying by the elementary charge, e. The wavelength is then found using the formula λ = hc/ΔE = hc / (4.8e), which corresponds to the expression in option C.</p>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The diagram shows the first four energy levels in an atom.</p>\n<p>Energy levels: <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=4\"></span> at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-3.9\\,\\mathrm{eV}\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=3\"></span> at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-5.8\\,\\mathrm{eV}\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=2\"></span> at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-8.7\\,\\mathrm{eV}\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=1\"></span> at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-17.2\\,\\mathrm{eV}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Which statement gives the correct wavelength for a transition from <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=4\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=2\"></span> in this atom?</p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\dfrac{ch}{(-8.7+3.9)e}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\dfrac{c(-8.7+3.9)e}{h}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\dfrac{ch}{(-3.9+8.7)e}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\dfrac{c(-3.9+8.7)e}{h}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
